## Background and Motivation

The `IPAddress` class contains a property `IsIPv6SiteLocal`, but the IPv6 site local range has been deprecated since 2004.

Since October 2005, a new range has been reserved by IETF to denote "Unique Local Addresses" (ULA) for use within private networks. It would be nice if `IPAddress` also had a property that checks for this range.

See also https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unique_local_address

## Proposed API

```csharp
namespace System.Net
{
    public class IPAddress
    {
        public bool IsIPv6UniqueLocal { get; }
    }
}
```

Where the property could be implemented as:

```csharp
public bool IsIPv6UniqueLocal
    => IsIPv6 && ((_numbers[0] & 0xFE00) == 0xFC00);
```

